1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,365
Centuries later, the Greek
writer Pausanias described a

2
00:00:03,365 --> 00:00:07,305
tradition that the battlefield
was not truly silent at night.

3
00:00:07,485 --> 00:00:11,925
People claimed that after dark they could
still hear the sounds of battle there.

4
00:00:12,205 --> 00:00:14,205
Horses, men fighting.

5
00:00:15,125 --> 00:00:19,385
The dead still fighting the war they
had already lost their lives in.

6
00:00:19,745 --> 00:00:21,665
There were other stories too.

7
00:00:22,425 --> 00:00:26,285
One tradition told of a mysterious
figure who appeared during the

8
00:00:26,285 --> 00:00:30,345
battle and killed Persians with a
farmer's plow before disappearing.

9
00:00:31,145 --> 00:00:34,345
And Herodotus recorded
another strange account.

10
00:00:34,345 --> 00:00:39,145
An Athenian soldier named Epizelus
claimed that during the fighting he saw a

11
00:00:39,145 --> 00:00:44,465
gigantic armed warrior pass beside him
and kill the man standing next to him.

12
00:00:45,085 --> 00:00:50,425
Epizelus survived, but he was left
blind despite having no visible wound.
